[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=14 format=3]

; Real dark Theme resource (GUI decluttering pass, 2026-08-17). Authored
; against the mockup's own dark tokens -- these are the *exact* values
; already scattered as inline `theme_override_colors`/`StyleBoxFlat`
; literals throughout `main.tscn` (verified by comparison, not guessed),
; centralised here so every control -- including the SpinBox/OptionButton/
; CheckBox/Button controls that previously fell back to `app_theme.tres`'s
; light-parchment chrome sitting on this dark shell -- resolves to one
; theme with no fallback to the light one. Supersedes `app_theme.tres` as
; both `Main`'s theme and the project-wide default (`project.godot`
; `gui/theme/custom`); `app_theme.tres` itself is untouched (still a real,
; working light Theme resource) but no longer wired into the live path.
;
; Tokens (GUI_SHELL_SCOPE.md's decluttering-pass section has the full
; rationale):
;   surface   #0d0e0f   panel/page background
;   viewport  #101112   map-viewport background (very slightly lighter)
;   hairline  rgba(255,255,255,.10)  panel borders
;   divider   rgba(255,255,255,.05)  in-panel row/section rules
;   border    rgba(255,255,255,.14)  input-control borders
;   text      #c8cbcd   primary label/body colour
;   emphasis  #e8ebec   hover/active text, wordmark
;   dim       #8d9296   secondary chrome (menu labels, group headers)
;   label     #5f6468   tertiary/hint text, disabled-state font colour
;   accent    #e0a34a   the one accent -- active nav row, focus rings,
;             PrimaryButton fill -- reserved for active/accent states only
;
; Font: still Godot's built-in default for both UI chrome and numeric
; fields. The mockup calls for an IBM-Plex-Mono-equivalent on numeric/data
; fields (seed, resolution, coordinates) distinct from the UI sans -- no
; such font asset exists in this repo yet (same real gap `app_theme.tres`'s
; own header already flagged for Fira Sans/Fira Code and never closed).
; Sourcing + licensing a real font file is left exactly as deferred as it
; already was, not silently dropped.

